1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,082
After a heavy rain, a cocoa grower has about thirty minutes to scout.

2
00:00:05,082 --> 00:00:07,485
Which blocks should they check first?

3
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:10,798
Guess wrong, and black pod spreads to healthy pods.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:19,031
Black pod is spread by rain splash, and it is estimated to cost twenty to thirty percent of global cocoa production.

5
00:00:19,031 --> 00:00:23,499
Heavy rain is already linked to lower yields in Ghana, Ecuador and Indonesia.

6
00:00:23,499 --> 00:00:30,521
In Malaysia, eighty-six percent of cocoa land is smallholdings, where advisers cannot visit every farm after every storm.

7
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:35,673
Growers already have photo apps, forecasts and paper logs.

8
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:41,469
But none of them turns it rained heavily into walk these blocks first, in the time you have.

9
00:00:41,469 --> 00:00:44,177
That empty corner is where KokoShield sits.

10
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:53,351
KokoShield Field Desk takes the rain reading, the farm's block map and past cases, and produces a ranked route sized to thirty minutes.

11
00:00:53,351 --> 00:00:58,522
Every stop shows why it is there, and the route works on a phone or as a printed checklist.

12
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:03,288
Scouts log each suspected pod with a note and a photo.

13
00:01:03,288 --> 00:01:09,098
The grower or an adviser then confirms or rules out every case, so only verified disease counts.

14
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:13,142
Our pilot is one cocoa farm in Tanjung Sepat.

15
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:21,277
Two scouts walk for the same thirty minutes, one on the ranked route and one on the usual round, then a follow-up check counts what each missed.

16
00:01:21,277 --> 00:01:27,152
We move on only if the ranked route finds more confirmed pods per hour in at least three of four rounds.

17
00:01:27,152 --> 00:01:29,356
The pilot costs twelve hundred ringgit.

18
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:35,864
Finding disease sooner means fewer pods lost and treatment only where it is needed.

19
00:01:35,864 --> 00:01:37,793
Growers use KokoShield for free.

20
00:01:37,793 --> 00:01:45,871
A cooperative or buyer pays seventy-five ringgit per farm per season, starting with a twenty-farm cluster in Sabah or Sarawak in 2027.

21
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:49,925
We are a team of five from Universiti Malaya.

22
00:01:49,925 --> 00:01:58,667
KokoShield helps cocoa growers find disease sooner after the rain, starting with one farm and built to travel to every cocoa region facing wetter seasons.
